WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:04.404
- Now you have members
of the security state or

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:07.907
former members like Petraeus,
like Panetta, like Kinzinger,

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:12.912
saying that if there
is a nuclear use by
Russia in Ukraine,

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we must get directly
involved in this war.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:21.021 align:start size:97% position:3%
We must now bomb every Russian
military asset in Ukraine,

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:24.391 align:start size:97% position:3%
sink every ship that Russia
has in the Black Sea.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:28.128 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is what very respected
people in the beltway

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.362
are calling for.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.765
So we could, this
could tip over into

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:35.368
a hot war in which we
are a full belligerent

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.870
at any minute.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.440
(smooth synth intro music)

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.912
I'm Dave Rubin, and
joining me today is

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.680
the founder of Craft Ventures

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.817
and one of the co-hosts
of the "All-In" podcast,

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:54.087
David Sachs, welcome back
to "The Rubin Report."

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.922
- Great to be with you
Dave, good to see you.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:59.092
- David, when I contacted
you a couple weeks ago

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.560
to come back on,

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.629 align:start size:97% position:3%
it was because you were
getting all sorts of people

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:06.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
very angry at you over
this Ukraine-Russia thing.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:09.169 align:start position:0%
And it's bizarre, at least from
where I sit, because to me,

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:12.372 align:start size:88% position:13%
you've been one of
kind of the most sober,

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.007
"Hey, let's not rush into war.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.642
What are we doing here?

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:19.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this costing us money?"
and all sorts of stuff.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.447
That's the voice
that you have been,

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.715
but I didn't even know
you really cared about

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.952
international relations to
this extent before that.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:29.255
So maybe for people
that don't know you

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.957 align:start size:88% position:13%
or why we're even having
this conversation,

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.459
maybe we should start there.

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:35.662
Why did you get involved
in this whole conversation?

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:38.164
- Well, I can't imagine an issue

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.233 align:start size:84% position:16%
that is more
important to all of us

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.135
than whether we get
in World War III,

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:44.437
and it was Biden himself,

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.639
it was Biden himself who
said just the other day

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:84% position:16%
that the United States
was at the risk of

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.978
getting into what he
called Armageddon.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.513
He said that we faced

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:56.082
the most serious risk of
getting into a nuclear war

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:58.251
since the Cuban Missile Crisis.

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.386 align:start size:88% position:13%
And the one time you
can really believe Biden

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.388
is when he's off
prompter, right?

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:05.091 align:start size:97% position:3%
He's saying things
spontaneously off the cuff.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:08.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I actually believe that
this is what he thinks

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.063 align:start position:0%
and these are the conversations
that are happening

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.531
inside the White House.

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:13.666 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so I think we all should
be very concerned about

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.635
where this war is leading us.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.537
In terms of my interest, I mean,

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.373
the foreign policy has been an
interest of mine for a while,

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.909
but when I saw what was
happening on this issue

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.878
and where it was leading,

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:28.715
and specifically we're in an
escalatory spiral with Russia,

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.817 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is, you know,
another nuclear power,

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.418
it's the country in the world

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.820
that has the most
nuclear weapons.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.922
It's really the only
country in the world

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.625 align:start size:88% position:13%
that can truly threaten
our own security

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:41.661
because of the sheer number
of ICBMs that they have.

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:44.931
This is the only Achilles
heel that we really have.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:48.368 align:start size:97% position:3%
Our military is so vastly more
powerful than anybody else.

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:49.602
No one can really touch us

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.471 align:start size:84% position:16%
except for this
one issue of ICBMs.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.339
So they do pose a
real threat to us.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.574 align:start size:84% position:16%
So we need to be
very concerned about

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.709 align:start size:84% position:16%
where this escalatory
spiral is headed.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.012
And look, my interest is
really just coming at it

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.781
from the point of view of
being a concerned American.

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:04.017
And I do this podcast called
"The All-In Pod" every week

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.752
where we talk about this issue

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:08.454
and for expressing
any concerns about

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.123
where this war is headed,

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:12.859
you're instantly denounced as
some sort of Putin apologist

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.762
or agent of the Kremlin
or something like that.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.197
And just to be completely clear,

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:20.333
I have no financial
dealings with Russia

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.302
or anyone from Russia.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.537
I invest in American startups.

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:29.542 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, you know, I have no
interest in this other than

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:32.779
coming out from the point of
view of a concerned American.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:35.114
- And for complete
transparency's sake,

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.817
you also were an
investor in Locals

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.852
and obviously then we merged
with Rumble and All Goods.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.321
- A very worthy startup.

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:43.890 align:start size:97% position:3%
But yes, these are the types
of, this is what I do is

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:47.026
I invest in startups,
in American companies.

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:48.261
- And David, I can
give you my word

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.495
I'm not a Russian operative,

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.064
so you're clear on my end.

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:54.801 align:start size:97% position:3%
Okay, so look, I actually have
not covered Russia-Ukraine

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.569
a ton on the show because

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.638 align:start size:88% position:13%
my general feeling is
there's so much going on

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:01.474 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the United States right now
domestically that is wrong.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:04.277
I've been just keeping my eye
on that a little bit more,

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:05.778 align:start size:81% position:19%
but my general
thoughts have been

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.947 align:start size:88% position:13%
you've got two sovereign
countries here.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:10.583
You can't invade a sovereign
country, but at the same time,

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.419
once he does it and the
guy with the big guns,

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.555 align:start size:97% position:3%
with the nukes, if you
don't give him an off ramp,

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:17.023
we could really be
in a lot of trouble.

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:19.259
And I think that's where you've
been going with all of this.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:22.462 align:start size:97% position:3%
Are you shocked the way
people have pushed back on,

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:25.999
"Hey, let's not go
to World War III?"

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.767 align:start size:88% position:13%
In your Newsweek
piece, you talked about

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.603
this confluence of now the
wokesters and the neocons

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:33.906
who you'd think have nothing
in common, how they're really

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.675
the driving force of
this whole thing now.

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:37.710 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right, well, let's
take an example.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.280
So Elon Musk proposed on Twitter

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.882
a simple straw man
for a peace deal.

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:46.252 align:start size:97% position:3%
It was a very, I think, a
pretty reasonable framework.

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:49.489 align:start size:97% position:3%
It basically said that,
listen, we will do elections

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:52.592 align:start size:97% position:3%
in these disputed territories
in eastern Ukraine,

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:55.328
not sham elections,
but elections under
the supervision of,

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:59.265 align:start size:84% position:16%
say, the United
Nations peacekeepers
and election monitors.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:02.235 align:start size:88% position:13%
We recognize that Crimea
is a fait accompli,

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:05.905
Russia annexed it 2014,
that ship has sailed.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:10.376 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you know, we
recognize that Ukraine

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:13.079 align:start size:97% position:3%
will not become part of
NATO, which Russia feels is

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:14.914
very threatening to
their own security,

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.783
but we can sell them weapons

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:17.850 align:start size:84% position:16%
and give them
security guarantees.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.585
That was roughly the proposal,

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:24.157
by the way, those rough
contours of a peace deal

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:28.127 align:start size:97% position:3%
have been suggested by many
experts for over a year

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:29.562
to resolve this crisis.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:31.164
But in any event,
my point is this,

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:33.933
that he was denounced by no
less than Zelenskyy himself

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:36.903
who took to Twitter
to basically say that

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:39.038 align:start size:84% position:16%
the mere suggestion
of a peace deal

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:42.942 align:start size:84% position:16%
was acting in
pro-Russian interests.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:45.178
So this is the point in the
debate that we've reached

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:48.247 align:start size:84% position:16%
is that if you raise
even the idea of

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:51.751 align:start size:97% position:3%
trying to find a diplomatic
solution to this war,

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:54.587 align:start size:84% position:16%
or if you bring up
any of the pre-history

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:57.223 align:start size:84% position:16%
to what happened
before February 24th,

00:05:57.223 --> 00:06:00.760
if you point out that
the West's desire for

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.329
NATO expansion right up
to Russia's front porch

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:08.167
might have played a role
in creating this conflict.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:12.805 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you bring up any idea that
that's not on board with,

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:16.075 align:start size:84% position:16%
I would say maximalist
Ukrainian demands

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:18.511 align:start size:88% position:13%
to take back every
square inch of territory

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:20.813
that they consider to be theirs,

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:23.683 align:start size:97% position:3%
then you are now pro-Russian
and a Kremlin agent.

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:27.120
- Where do you think, or
what do you think that

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.855
that says about Zelenskyy?

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:31.224
That he obviously
is outgunned here,

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:32.992 align:start size:84% position:16%
he's getting a crazy
amount of money

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:35.294 align:start size:84% position:16%
and all sorts of
weapons and technology

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:36.896 align:start size:88% position:13%
and everything else
from all over the world,

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:38.364 align:start size:81% position:19%
but as you say,
he's maximalist on

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:40.867 align:start size:84% position:16%
"get the hell outta
here, guy with nukes."

00:06:40.867 --> 00:06:42.602
And that doesn't seem normally

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:45.371 align:start size:97% position:3%
how the symmetry of something
like this would play out.

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:47.607
As Kamala Harris said,
Russia big Ukraine small.

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:51.544
- Well, so I think at the
beginning of the wars,

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:54.113
Zelenskyy himself was
floating peace deals

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:57.016
that were not dissimilar
from what Elon suggested.

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:58.751
He said that he was open to

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:01.854
taking the issue of NATO
expansion off the table.

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:03.823 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then unfortunately
Boris Johnson

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:07.126
went to Ukraine in April
and killed that peace deal.

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:08.628
And now since then,

00:07:08.628 --> 00:07:11.364
there have been so many
losses on both sides,

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:13.966 align:start size:97% position:3%
but especially the Ukrainians
have suffered so much

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:17.770
that there's no longer any
appetite for a peace deal.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:21.307
I understand that this
is what happens in war

00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:24.744
is that people experience so
much loss, so much devastation

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:27.413
that they get more dug
in on their position,

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:30.283 align:start size:88% position:13%
and Zelenskyy is
following a position of

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:34.387
Ukrainian nationalism, that
is what his country supports.

00:07:34.387 --> 00:07:37.089 align:start size:88% position:13%
Now, I think the
mistake would be for us,

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:38.991
even though I think
we sympathize with

00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:42.462
their Ukrainian nationalism,
their desire for sovereignty,

00:07:42.462 --> 00:07:44.797
I think that we have to consider

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:46.566 align:start size:84% position:16%
what's in America's
own interest.

00:07:46.566 --> 00:07:47.800
Zelenskyy is representing

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.435
what's in his own
country's interest,

00:07:49.435 --> 00:07:51.871
what's in Ukraine's interest.

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:53.506
But we need to think about

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:54.907 align:start size:84% position:16%
what's in the United
States' interest.

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:56.409
And the fact of the matter is

00:07:56.409 --> 00:07:59.278
we are getting increasingly
drawn in to this conflict

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:02.014
in a deeper and deeper
way to the point where

00:08:02.014 --> 00:08:05.418
now we actually might face
the risk of a nuclear war.

00:08:05.418 --> 00:08:06.919
And I think it's about time that

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:09.856 align:start size:88% position:13%
somebody on the American
side started saying,

00:08:09.856 --> 00:08:13.359
"Listen, we understand the
Ukrainian position on this.

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:15.995 align:start size:97% position:3%
We sympathize with you, we're
willing to give you aid,

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:18.130
but what are our limits?

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.832 align:start size:84% position:16%
What is in the
American interest?"

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:21.868
And those are the questions
we'd be asking right now.

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:23.870 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Do you think
this administration

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.339
has the American
interest at heart?

00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:29.408 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, at the
beginning of the war,

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:32.678
Biden said some sensible things.

00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:35.815
So for example, what he said
is that the U.S. would not

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:38.918
get directly involved in a
shooting war with Russia.

00:08:38.918 --> 00:08:41.988
He understood and said that
could cause World War III,

00:08:41.988 --> 00:08:43.456
we're not messing
around with that.

00:08:43.456 --> 00:08:46.859 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so, for example, he vetoed
the idea of a no fly zone,

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:50.796 align:start size:97% position:3%
which hardliners, you know,
the Twitter mob wanted.

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:53.399 align:start size:84% position:16%
And various
congressional elites,

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:54.901
Lindsey Graham and
so forth wanted.

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:56.335
Yeah, that was a smart decision.

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:58.371
Also, when Lester Holt asked him

00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:00.573
in a press interview at the
very beginning of the war,

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:02.341 align:start size:88% position:13%
he said, "Mr. President,
what if there's

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:04.010
Americans trapped
behind enemy lines,

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:06.078
would you send in our
troops to go get them?"

00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:09.115
And Biden said no,
even in that case

00:09:09.115 --> 00:09:12.251 align:start size:88% position:13%
we will not get directly
involved in this war.

00:09:12.251 --> 00:09:14.287
He didn't let the
press goad him into

00:09:14.287 --> 00:09:16.822
a direct American involvement.

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:18.157
But the problem is that

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:20.593
since then we've been
on a slippery slope

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:22.628 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we've begotten
more and more involved.

00:09:22.628 --> 00:09:24.497
So for example, you've now had

00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:27.500 align:start size:88% position:13%
administration officials
brag to publications

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.869
like the New York Times
and the Washington Post

00:09:29.869 --> 00:09:32.939 align:start position:0%
about killing Russian generals,
providing the intelligence

00:09:32.939 --> 00:09:35.374 align:start size:84% position:16%
that paints the
target on their back,

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:38.377
about providing the
intelligence, the
artillery spotting

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:41.147
to sink the Moskva, which
is the Russian flagship.

00:09:41.147 --> 00:09:42.548 align:start size:88% position:13%
You've had
administration officials

00:09:42.548 --> 00:09:44.717
bragging about the
role they played in

00:09:44.717 --> 00:09:46.185 align:start size:84% position:16%
this recent Ukrainian
counter offense.

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:49.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
Basically, the Ukrainians
presented plans

00:09:49.021 --> 00:09:50.523
to the American generals.

00:09:50.523 --> 00:09:52.358
The American said these
plans aren't good enough.

00:09:52.358 --> 00:09:53.859
They hand corrected them,
sent them back to Ukraine.

00:09:53.859 --> 00:09:56.996
And they're bragging about
this in the New York Times.

00:09:56.996 --> 00:10:00.733
We also keep appropriating
them more and more money,

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:03.603 align:start size:97% position:3%
more and more weapons and more
and more advanced weapons.

00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:06.405
And so we are getting
more and more involved.

00:10:06.405 --> 00:10:09.208 align:start size:97% position:3%
There also was a New York
