it in January,

00:29:12.650 --> 00:29:14.319
the administration
refused to do it,

00:29:14.319 --> 00:29:15.854
if we had done that,

00:29:15.854 --> 00:29:17.922 align:start size:88% position:13%
I do not believe
there'd be a war today.

00:29:17.922 --> 00:29:20.825
- Do you think the march
for the NATO expansion,

00:29:20.825 --> 00:29:22.961
for Ukraine to get in
NATO is gonna continue?

00:29:22.961 --> 00:29:26.131
- Yes, I mean, so here's
the tell on this is that

00:29:26.131 --> 00:29:28.233
the very same people who say

00:29:28.233 --> 00:29:31.002
this war has nothing to
do with NATO expansion,

00:29:31.002 --> 00:29:33.204
people like McFall
and various others,

00:29:33.204 --> 00:29:35.540
in the next breath they will say

00:29:35.540 --> 00:29:37.942 align:start size:88% position:13%
we cannot take NATO
expansion off the table,

00:29:37.942 --> 00:29:39.611
that is non-negotiable.

00:29:39.611 --> 00:29:41.112
Well, hold on a second.

00:29:41.112 --> 00:29:43.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
If this war has nothing
to do with NATO expansion,

00:29:43.214 --> 00:29:44.716
why can't you take
it off the table?

00:29:44.716 --> 00:29:46.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
This war has everything
to do with NATO expansion.

00:29:46.284 --> 00:29:51.289 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is a crusade that
goes back many years, okay?

00:29:52.490 --> 00:29:54.359
Our state department
has been engaged on

00:29:54.359 --> 00:29:56.461 align:start size:84% position:16%
this long term
project to basically

00:29:56.461 --> 00:29:59.063
bring NATO right up
to Russia's borders.

00:29:59.063 --> 00:30:02.901
And that has provoked a very
strong response from Russia.

00:30:02.901 --> 00:30:04.969 align:start size:88% position:13%
By the way, I'm not
justifying the invasion.

00:30:04.969 --> 00:30:07.071
It was wrong, it was criminal.

00:30:07.071 --> 00:30:09.107 align:start size:81% position:19%
But the fact of
the matter is that

00:30:09.107 --> 00:30:12.911
we could have diffused this
crisis before the war began

00:30:12.911 --> 00:30:14.445
if we were willing
to use diplomacy.

00:30:14.445 --> 00:30:16.815
And I believe that even today

00:30:16.815 --> 00:30:19.684 align:start size:84% position:16%
we could try to
engage in diplomacy,

00:30:19.684 --> 00:30:21.586 align:start size:84% position:16%
take NATO expansion
off the table,

00:30:21.586 --> 00:30:23.922
recognize that Crimea
is a fait accompli,

00:30:23.922 --> 00:30:26.691
and then support some sort
of negotiated settlement

00:30:26.691 --> 00:30:28.126
over the Donbas region.

00:30:28.126 --> 00:30:30.461
If we were just to agree
to those three things,

00:30:30.461 --> 00:30:34.432 align:start size:97% position:3%
which seem very sensible,
America has no vital interest,

00:30:34.432 --> 00:30:37.669 align:start size:97% position:3%
and any of those three
things that would supersede

00:30:37.669 --> 00:30:40.839
or that would necessitate us
to get into a war with Russia,

00:30:40.839 --> 00:30:42.841
if we were just to
do those things,

00:30:42.841 --> 00:30:45.443 align:start size:97% position:3%
I believe there's a good
chance we could end this war.

00:30:45.443 --> 00:30:48.246
- And in some ways, is
it almost a moot point

00:30:48.246 --> 00:30:50.448
whether they were to
get in NATO or not?

00:30:50.448 --> 00:30:53.384 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because if we're in an endless
war that we're funding,

00:30:53.384 --> 00:30:55.687
whether they're in it or
not, we're kind of in it.

00:30:55.687 --> 00:30:56.888
That's the point, right?

00:30:56.888 --> 00:30:59.057
- Well, a couple of things.

00:30:59.057 --> 00:31:00.358 align:start size:84% position:16%
So first of all,
obviously Ukraine is

00:31:00.358 --> 00:31:01.826
more than capable of
defending themselves

00:31:01.826 --> 00:31:03.595 align:start size:97% position:3%
if we sell them weapons
without them being in NATO.

00:31:03.595 --> 00:31:05.296
So if this war has
proven anything,

00:31:05.296 --> 00:31:06.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's that Ukraine doesn't
need to be in NATO.

00:31:06.831 --> 00:31:09.968
Furthermore, however,
we need to think about

00:31:09.968 --> 00:31:11.936 align:start size:81% position:19%
is it really in
America's interest

00:31:11.936 --> 00:31:13.204
for Ukraine to be in NATO?

00:31:13.204 --> 00:31:16.674
Because if Ukraine were in NATO,

00:31:16.674 --> 00:31:19.010
they would have an article
five guarantee, which means

00:31:19.010 --> 00:31:21.412
the next time that they
get in a war with Russia,

00:31:21.412 --> 00:31:23.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they will, 'cause
that feud's been going on

00:31:23.715 --> 00:31:25.216
for hundreds of years,

00:31:25.216 --> 00:31:27.085
we will be instantly obligated
to get in a war with Russia.

00:31:27.085 --> 00:31:30.955 align:start position:0%
This is why historically we
have not brought them into NATO.

00:31:30.955 --> 00:31:32.523
This is why there
was reluctance.

00:31:32.523 --> 00:31:35.593
We stated our intention
to do so back in 2008

00:31:35.593 --> 00:31:37.729
and we were slowly
building towards it.

00:31:37.729 --> 00:31:39.163 align:start size:84% position:16%
But there was
always concern that

00:31:39.163 --> 00:31:42.233
if we were actually to
bring Ukraine into NATO,

00:31:42.233 --> 00:31:44.535 align:start size:97% position:3%
it would obligate us to
get into a war with Russia.

00:31:44.535 --> 00:31:46.738 align:start size:84% position:16%
And by the way, if you
like the feeling of

00:31:46.738 --> 00:31:49.574
living with a nuclear threat,

00:31:49.574 --> 00:31:51.376
remember when I was a kid,

00:31:51.376 --> 00:31:54.345
we lived under this threat
of nuclear annihilation.

00:31:54.345 --> 00:31:56.514
We had movies like "The
Day After" that showed

00:31:56.514 --> 00:31:58.416
what it was like if we
got in a nuclear war.

00:31:58.416 --> 00:32:00.585
I remember that, as a kid,
it was not a good feeling

00:32:00.585 --> 00:32:03.655 align:start position:0%
to grow up living under the
shadow of nuclear annihilation.

00:32:03.655 --> 00:32:05.123
We solved that problem.

00:32:05.123 --> 00:32:08.092
We won the Cold War in
1991, and now it is back.

00:32:08.092 --> 00:32:09.260
It is back.

00:32:09.260 --> 00:32:10.495
We have been living this year

00:32:10.495 --> 00:32:12.297
under the shadow
of a nuclear war.

00:32:12.297 --> 00:32:15.033
So listen, if you like that
feeling, then by all means

00:32:15.033 --> 00:32:18.369 align:start size:88% position:13%
bring Ukraine into NATO
as soon as possible

00:32:18.369 --> 00:32:19.671
because we will
be forever living

00:32:19.671 --> 00:32:22.006
under the threat of
nuclear annihilation

00:32:22.006 --> 00:32:24.676
because again, article
five will trigger us

00:32:24.676 --> 00:32:26.711 align:start size:84% position:16%
to get into a nuclear
war with Russia.

00:32:26.711 --> 00:32:29.547
So it is a foolish idea, it
was always a foolish idea.

00:32:29.547 --> 00:32:32.817 align:start size:97% position:3%
It is not in American interest
to bring Ukraine into NATO

00:32:32.817 --> 00:32:35.820
and yet these crusaders
in the state department

00:32:35.820 --> 00:32:37.355
have made it their mission.

00:32:37.355 --> 00:32:39.891 align:start size:88% position:13%
And we need to take
that issue off the table

00:32:39.891 --> 00:32:41.292
as soon as possible.

00:32:41.292 --> 00:32:43.494
- Sachs, that is a primo close.

00:32:43.494 --> 00:32:46.030
However, I am gonna ask
you one other thing,

00:32:46.030 --> 00:32:48.433 align:start position:0%
but I do wanna just give a shout
out to your Newsweek piece,

00:32:48.433 --> 00:32:50.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was called "The
Neocons and the Woke Left

00:32:50.501 --> 00:32:54.639 align:start size:97% position:3%
are Joining Hands and Leading
Us to Woke War Three."

00:32:54.639 --> 00:32:57.208
We'll also link to that down
below. Now I just wanna ask you

00:32:57.208 --> 00:33:00.078
something sort of personal
on all of this, which is that

00:33:00.078 --> 00:33:01.746
you're obviously doing all
right, you don't need to be

00:33:01.746 --> 00:33:04.182
taking the slings and
arrows for this thing,

00:33:04.182 --> 00:33:05.416
yet you're doing it.

00:33:05.416 --> 00:33:06.884
And it's interesting to
me, as I said before,

00:33:06.884 --> 00:33:08.319
that suddenly I'm finding

00:33:08.319 --> 00:33:09.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
the people that I'm
interested in politically

00:33:09.988 --> 00:33:12.390
are tech people and
business people.

00:33:12.390 --> 00:33:14.325
They're not the politics people.

00:33:14.325 --> 00:33:17.962 align:start size:88% position:13%
But it can't be all
fun doing this for you,

00:33:17.962 --> 00:33:20.098
even though I know you care
about it and all that stuff.

00:33:20.098 --> 00:33:21.733
But yeah, you know, you're
putting your neck out there,

00:33:21.733 --> 00:33:23.935
you have businesses
and all those things.

00:33:23.935 --> 00:33:25.403
- Dave, if I saw more people

00:33:25.403 --> 00:33:27.105 align:start size:97% position:3%
who are part of the foreign
policy establishment

00:33:27.105 --> 00:33:29.941
speaking out and being
just a little bit brave,

00:33:29.941 --> 00:33:32.944 align:start size:97% position:3%
willing to basically be
called a pro-Russian puppet

00:33:32.944 --> 00:33:34.679 align:start size:84% position:16%
to advocate for
diplomacy and peace,

00:33:34.679 --> 00:33:36.814 align:start size:88% position:13%
it wouldn't be on
people like me to do it.

00:33:36.814 --> 00:33:38.483
But the fact of the matter is,

00:33:38.483 --> 00:33:40.218
I don't care what
these people say.

00:33:40.218 --> 00:33:43.588
I have, I've told you before,
I've got no business interest.

00:33:43.588 --> 00:33:45.623 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm not part of this foreign
policy establishment.

00:33:45.623 --> 00:33:48.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not beholden to their
sort of insider club.

00:33:48.059 --> 00:33:51.295
And you know what, if we
get in a war with Russia,

00:33:51.295 --> 00:33:52.830
then that's gonna interrupt

00:33:52.830 --> 00:33:55.133
the operations of
my venture fund.

00:33:55.133 --> 00:33:57.068
Let's just say that, okay?

00:33:57.068 --> 00:33:59.137 align:start position:0%
We're gonna have much more
important things to worry about

00:33:59.137 --> 00:34:00.638
then my next star investment.

00:34:00.638 --> 00:34:02.607 align:start size:97% position:3%
So it's my obligation as an
American citizen to speak out.

00:34:02.607 --> 00:34:05.209
I believe that is why
Elon Musk spoke out.

00:34:05.209 --> 00:34:08.046
He is a very informed
person, by the way.

00:34:08.046 --> 00:34:10.081 align:start size:84% position:16%
He knows people
all over the world.

00:34:10.081 --> 00:34:12.717
He is very concerned about
this, just read his tweets.

00:34:12.717 --> 00:34:14.352
He's taking a lot of flack too.

00:34:14.352 --> 00:34:16.654
Bill Ackman recently spoke out,

00:34:16.654 --> 00:34:18.923 align:start size:97% position:3%
who, by the way, we've been
debating each other on Twitter

00:34:18.923 --> 00:34:20.191
for a while about this.

00:34:20.191 --> 00:34:21.726
And he recently spoke out.

00:34:21.726 --> 00:34:24.028
So you're seeing more and
more people speak out.

00:34:24.028 --> 00:34:26.197
Their only interest here is that

00:34:26.197 --> 00:34:28.599
they are concerned about
America and they do not see

00:34:28.599 --> 00:34:31.369
people in the foreign policy
establishment and politicians

00:34:31.369 --> 00:34:33.504
speaking out the
way they should be.

00:34:33.504 --> 00:34:35.440 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that includes
the Republican party,

00:34:35.440 --> 00:34:38.276 align:start position:0%
who frankly has completely
dropped the ball on this issue.

00:34:38.276 --> 00:34:40.445
- David, I always tell people

00:34:40.445 --> 00:34:41.979
if we were just a
little bit braver,

00:34:41.979 --> 00:34:42.980
things would be a lot better.

00:34:42.980 --> 00:34:44.849
So, I love that finish.

00:34:44.849 --> 00:34:46.584
Good talking to you, my friend.

00:34:46.584 --> 00:34:47.685
- Great to see you, thanks Dave.

00:34:47.685 --> 00:34:49.187
